cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "qualembed: Embedding-Based Semantic Measurement and Calibration for Survey and Qualitative Text"
message: >-
  If you use this package, please cite both the software and the paper
  it was written for.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Muta
    given-names: Toshizumi
    email: toshizumi.muta@psycholo.studio
    affiliation: Psycholo Studio
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-09-19
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.22682901
license: GPL-3.0-or-later
repository-code: "https://github.com/PsycholoStudio/qualembed"
abstract: >-
  A thin, auditable toolkit for measuring the meaning of nominal and narrative
  survey responses in the semantic space of large language model embeddings.
  One request layer over three commercial providers, an analysis layer of
  permutation-based statistics, and the displays the accompanying paper uses.
keywords:
  - text embeddings
  - large language models
  - survey research
  - open-ended responses
  - nominal data
  - semantic similarity
  - R
references:
  - type: article
    title: >-
      Embedding qualitative data in LLM semantic space: A tutorial on
      conceptualization, measurement, and validation
    authors:
      - family-names: Muta
        given-names: Toshizumi
    year: 2026
